@xiaoyuyu6420/dsh-backup README · dsh-backup：**Your entire DeepSeek Harness (DSH) workspace lives in one folder: `~/.dsh`. One failed upgrade, one accidental delete, one new laptop — without a backup, sessions, settings and skills are all gone. dsh-backup gives them back with one command.**

```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add @xiaoyuyu6420/dsh-backup   # install

@xiaoyuyu6420/dsh-backup README · restart dsh web, then type:：- 🔐 **Credentials never leave this machine** — API keys / tokens are redacted by default; plaintext lives only in the local vault. For more, opt into password-encrypted backups (AES-256-GCM).
- ↩️ **Restore never overwrites silently** — the current data is auto-snapshotted and the write-back is previewed first; a failed restore rolls back automatically.
- 🧭 **You'll know what to do from the start** — a three-step onboarding plus one plain-sentence explanation per advanced feature; three tabs (Backup / Restore / Settings) with a single primary action: "Back up now".

@xiaoyuyu6420/dsh-backup README · Install：Requires macOS / Linux / Windows 10+ (ships `tar`) and DSH `0.1.1-rc.2`+ (the 0.1.1 / 0.1.2 / 0.1.5 / 0.1.6 / 0.1.7 trains are all tested; the 0.2.0 and 0.2.1 trains are supported since 0.13.2 / 0.14.0 — see the [compatibility matrix](docs/compatibility.md) for the current status).

```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add @xiaoyuyu6420/dsh-backup

